    "result_text": "I added an \"Export CSV\" button (`data-testid=\"export-people\"`) to the people bar, and `bin/e2e` passes.\n\nThe change is one new file, `src/main/frontend/features/people/export.slot.tsx`. The app picks it up and shows it on the people bar automatically. Clicking the button saves a file named `people-<sheet>.csv` containing:\n- the header line `name,grade,retired-from,due-total`\n- one line per person in the order they were added, including retired people even when the list on screen hides them\n- each person's grade in force on the sheet's today, their retired-from date or an empty field, and their due-total exactly as the row shows it (`n/a` when there's no rate)\n\nA value containing a comma, a quote or a line break is wrapped in double quotes, with any quote inside doubled. Every line ends with a line feed.\n\nThe file is built in the browser from the people and claims the screen already has loaded, using the same due-total calculation as the person rows. So I didn't add a server endpoint, change stored data or write audit records.",
